The issue involves Dart syntax highlighting breaking when an empty block comment is present (`/**/`). As seen in the bug scenario images, the code syntax highlighting appears incorrectly due to the handling of comments in the highlighting logic.

This occurs because the highlighter does not properly handle empty comments or comments at the start/end of the code block, causing it to misinterpret the code.

### Bug Location

The issue originates from the way comments are processed within the Dart language definition in `src/languages/dart.js`. The code snippet specifically related to comments is:

```javascript
